second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"Who is Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet's spouse?\", \"slot_hint\": \"person\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 96, \"text\": \"**SCOTTISH JUDICIAL COMMUNITY ABUZZ AS LORD KENNET TIES THE KNOT WITH SOCIETY MATRON EMMA WOOD**\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 98, \"end\": 328, \"text\": \"Edinburgh, Scotland - In a surprise move, Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet, a respected Scottish advocate, legal scholar, and judge, has married Emma Wood, wife of Sir Nicholas Brooksbank, 3rd Baronet, in a private ceremony last weekend.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 329, \"end\": 456, \"text\": \"The union, which has sent shockwaves through Scotland's legal and social circles, was confirmed by sources close to the couple.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 457, \"end\": 612, \"text\": \"Lord Kennet, 75, has been a prominent figure in Scottish jurisprudence for decades, while Emma Wood, 73, is a well-known society matron and philanthropist.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 613, \"end\": 724, \"text\": \"\\\"I'm absolutely delighted for Robert and Emma,\\\" said Lady Margaret Macpherson, a longtime friend of the couple.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 725, \"end\": 750, \"text\": \"\\\"They're a perfect match.\"}, \"D1S7\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 751, \"end\": 857, \"text\": \"Both are highly respected in their respective fields, and they share a deep commitment to public service.\\\"\"}, \"D1S8\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 858, \"end\": 968, \"text\": \"The ceremony, attended by close friends and family, took place at the historic Dalhousie Castle in Midlothian.\"}, \"D1S9\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 969, \"end\": 1107, \"text\": \"Guests described the atmosphere as \\\"intimate and joyful,\\\" with Lord Kennet beaming with happiness as he exchanged vows with his new bride.\"}, \"D1S10\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1108, \"end\": 1299, \"text\": \"Emma Wood, who has been married to Sir Nicholas Brooksbank for over 40 years, has been a pillar of Scottish society, known for her tireless work on behalf of various charitable organizations.\"}, \"D1S11\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1300, \"end\": 1398, \"text\": \"Her marriage to Lord Kennet marks a new chapter in her life, one that she is eager to embark upon.\"}, \"D1S12\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1399, \"end\": 1484, \"text\": \"\\\"I'm thrilled to be starting this new journey with Robert,\\\" Emma said in a statement.\"}, \"D1S13\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1485, \"end\": 1582, \"text\": \"\\\"We share a deep love for Scotland and a commitment to making a positive impact on our community.\"}, \"D1S14\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1583, \"end\": 1632, \"text\": \"I'm excited to see what the future holds for us.\\\"\"}, \"D1S15\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1633, \"end\": 1768, \"text\": \"Lord Kennet, who has written extensively on Scottish law and history, has been a vocal advocate for judicial reform and social justice.\"}, \"D1S16\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1769, \"end\": 1904, \"text\": \"His marriage to Emma Wood is seen as a union of two like-minded individuals who will continue to make a difference in Scottish society.\"}, \"D1S17\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 1905, \"end\": 2070, \"text\": \"According to data from the Scottish Courts and Tribunals Service, Lord Kennet has presided over some of the most high-profile cases in recent Scottish legal history.\"}, \"D1S18\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2071, \"end\": 2172, \"text\": \"His expertise and fairness have earned him widespread respect among his peers and the general public.\"}, \"D1S19\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"start\": 2173, \"end\": 2269, \"text\": \"As news of the marriage spread, tributes poured in from across the legal and social communities.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 36, \"text\": \"Here is a potential Wikipedia entry:\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 38, \"end\": 67, \"text\": \"**Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet**\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 69, \"end\": 157, \"text\": \"Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet (died 1748) was a Scottish advocate, legal scholar, and judge.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 158, \"end\": 183, \"text\": \"**Early Life and Career**\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 185, \"end\": 261, \"text\": \"Bruce was born into a prominent Scottish family and pursued a career in law.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 262, \"end\": 344, \"text\": \"He became an advocate in 1696 and quickly gained a reputation as a skilled lawyer.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 345, \"end\": 470, \"text\": \"In 1714, he was appointed as a judge of the Court of Session, Scotland's highest civil court, and took the title Lord Kennet.\"}, \"D2S8\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 471, \"end\": 488, \"text\": \"**Personal Life**\"}, \"D2S9\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 490, \"end\": 545, \"text\": \"Lord Kennet married Helen Abercromby, who died in 1786.\"}, \"D2S10\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 546, \"end\": 698, \"text\": \"This marriage is documented in several sources, including the Scottish National Dictionary of Biography and the Oxford Dictionary of National Biography.\"}, \"D2S11\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 699, \"end\": 705, \"text\": \"[1][2]\"}, \"D2S12\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 707, \"end\": 721, \"text\": \"**References**\"}, \"D2S13\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 723, \"end\": 769, \"text\": \"[1] Scottish National Dictionary of Biography.\"}, \"D2S14\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 770, \"end\": 777, \"text\": \"(2007).\"}, \"D2S15\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 778, \"end\": 805, \"text\": \"Bruce, Robert, Lord Kennet.\"}, \"D2S16\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 806, \"end\": 926, \"text\": \"Retrieved from <https:\\\\/\\\\/www.oxforddnb.com\\\\/view\\\\/10.1093\\\\/ref:odnb\\\\/9780198614128.001.0001\\\\/odnb-9780198614128-e-3764>\"}, \"D2S17\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 928, \"end\": 972, \"text\": \"[2] Oxford Dictionary of National Biography.\"}, \"D2S18\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 973, \"end\": 980, \"text\": \"(2004).\"}, \"D2S19\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 981, \"end\": 1011, \"text\": \"Bruce, Robert, Lord Kennet (d.\"}, \"D2S20\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"start\": 1012, \"end\": 1018, \"text\": \"1748).\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"card_id\": \"d2:c0\", \"entity\": \"spouse\", \"scope\": \"Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet\", \"claim\": \"Robert Bruce, Lord Kennet's spouse is Helen Abercromby.\", \"answer\": \"Helen Abercromby\", \"quote\": \"Lord Kennet married Helen Abercromby, who died in 1786.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"Emma Wood\",